>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `threaded_cong_ss`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.threaded_cong_ss : thm list -> simpExtLib.ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Creates an extension fragment containing threaded congruence rules.
The fragment must be installed in a `simpExtLib.simpset`, not an ordinary
`simpLib.simpset`.

`threaded_cong_ss ths` is an anonymous fragment of congruence rules,
normalised in the same way as the `congs` field of `simpExtLib.SSFRAG`.
Add it with `simpExtLib.++`, or pass it through `simpExtLib.SF` after
naming/registering it in the extension fragment registry.

A threaded rule may name an intermediate result only in a later
antecedent, rather than in the conclusion's right-hand side. For example,
`Q` and `g` below are results of the first two recursive simplifications;
the third antecedent consumes them to produce the final result `h`:

``` hol4
   |- (!x. P x = Q x) ==> (!x. Q x ==> (f x = g x)) ==>
      (!x. (Q x /\ g x) = h x) ==>
      ((?x. P x /\ f x) = (?x. h x))
```

Applied higher-order result variables are beta-reduced in the rebuilt
right-hand side after instantiation. This does not beta-reduce the
original term on the left-hand side. These extensions apply only to
rules in `threaded_cong_ss`; the `congs` field of `simpExtLib.SSFRAG`
and `simpExtLib.Cong`, like `simpLib.SSFRAG` and `simpLib.Cong`, use
ordinary congruence handling.

### Failure

Never fails. Malformed congruence rules can cause later addition of the
fragment to a simpset, or simplification with that simpset, to fail.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val threaded = prove(
      “(!x:'a. P x = Q x) ==> (!x:'a. Q x ==> (f x = g x)) ==>
       (!x:'a. (Q x /\ g x) = h x) ==>
       ((?x:'a. P x /\ f x) = (?x:'a. h x))”,
      DISCH_TAC THEN DISCH_TAC THEN
      DISCH_THEN (fn rebuilt => REWRITE_TAC [GSYM rebuilt]) THEN
      AP_TERM_TAC THEN ABS_TAC THEN ASM_REWRITE_TAC [] THEN
      ASM_CASES_TAC “Q (x:'a) : bool” THEN RES_TAC THEN ASM_REWRITE_TAC []);
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss : simpExtLib.simpset = simpExtLib.++
     (ext_bool_ss, simpExtLib.threaded_cong_ss [threaded]);
>> simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV ss [ASSUME “!y:'a. bnd y ==> (bdy y <=> bdy' y)”]
     “?x:'a. bnd x /\ bdy x”;
```

